# Flat Dense Triplet 5 FPS Evaluation

This notebook records the benchmark for the trained flat dense triplet model at
5 FPS. The benchmark compares the learned model against deterministic motion
baselines on the same held-out MABe test windows.

## Evaluation contract

The recorded result comes from:

```text
outputs/evaluations/flat_dense_triplet_5fps/benchmark_16_24/results.jsonl
```

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Source FPS | 30 |
| Frame step | 6 |
| Effective FPS | 5 |
| Observation | 16 frames / 3.2 seconds |
| Prediction | 24 frames / 4.8 seconds |
| Windows | 1,000 |
| Seed | 42 |
| Checkpoint | `checkpoints/flat_dense_triplet_5fps/flat_best.pt` |
| Checkpoint epoch | 34 |
| Validation loss | -6.700201 |

Motion groups use `mean_keypoint_speed_px_s` thresholds fitted from training
windows:

| Group | Test windows | Rule |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Low | 311 | speed <= 16.665 px/s |
| Medium | 370 | 16.665 < speed <= 40.710 px/s |
| High | 319 | speed > 40.710 px/s |

## Aggregate metrics

All metrics below are means over the evaluated windows and are lower-is-better.
This snapshot was generated before p50/p99 quantile logging was added. Re-run
the benchmark at the end of this notebook to append a fresh record containing
`metric_quantiles` and `metric_quantiles_by_motion`.

| Method | cADE px | cFDE px | kADE px | kFDE px | CVE px/s | KVE px/s | BHE deg | BFK-ADE px | BFK-FDE px | BLE px | SOE deg | ROE |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Persistence | 42.579 | 70.636 | 47.081 | 76.432 | 28.690 | 36.640 | 27.013 | 47.179 | 76.604 | 7.590 | 30.730 | 0.181 |
