## Centroid FDE by motion group

| Motion group | Persistence | Rigid CV | Keypoint CV | Social Attention |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Low | 5.073 px | 16.793 px | 16.793 px | 122.769 px |
| Medium | 34.914 px | 58.075 px | 58.075 px | 163.423 px |
| High | 175.988 px | 287.824 px | 287.824 px | 214.396 px |

## Interpretation

Persistence remains the strongest baseline for this run. The learned flat model
is worse than persistence on every aggregate metric, including trajectory
metrics (`cADE`, `cFDE`, `kADE`, `kFDE`), first-derivative motion metrics
(`CVE`, `KVE`), pose (`BHE`), body-frame keypoint placement (`BFK-*`), structure
(`BLE`, `SOE`), and ordering (`ROE`).

The high-motion slice is the most useful diagnostic slice. It shows that longer
5 FPS windows make persistence less trivial, but the trained model still has not
learned a better rollout policy. This suggests the next experiments should focus
on whether the architecture can model a simpler target before adding more graph
complexity: single-mouse dense keypoints and within-mouse dense triplets.

## Reprint the benchmark tables

Use this cell to reprint the Rich benchmark tables from the latest JSONL record.
If the latest record includes quantiles, each method cell includes mean, p50,
and p99 together.

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import sys

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src").exists())
os.environ.setdefault("MPLCONFIGDIR", str(repo_root / "outputs/matplotlib"))
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

from benchmark_report import print_benchmark_tables

result_path = repo_root / "outputs/evaluations/flat_dense_triplet_5fps/benchmark_16_24/results.jsonl"
record = json.loads(result_path.read_text().splitlines()[-1])
print_benchmark_tables(record)
```

## Re-run the benchmark

Use this to append a fresh benchmark record with mean, p50, and p99 summaries.

```sh
python src/benchmark.py --config src/config/benchmark__flat_dense_triplet_5fps.yml
```
